## Project context for estimation

This project (mock3) contains two independent codelines, each with a single ticket:

- **mocka** (`/home/bradleyjerome/projects/mock3/mock-a`) — MOCK3-1: Riders aged exactly 65 are charged the adult fare. The bug is in `src/fares.ts`: `fareFor` uses `rider.age > 65` where it should use `>=`. The doc-comment already states "Riders aged 65 AND OVER pay the concession fare." The existing test suite (`test/fares.test.ts`) covers ages 30, 8, and 70 but has no test at the exact age-65 boundary. The fix is a single comparison-operator change plus one new test case.

- **mockb** (`/home/bradleyjerome/projects/mock3/mock-b`) — MOCK3-2: The departure board omits the final stop. The bug is in `src/schedule.ts`: `formatStops` loops `i < stops.length - 1`, dropping the last stop. `totalMinutes` already references `stops[stops.length - 1]`, confirming the intent. The existing test suite (`test/schedule.test.ts`) checks for arrow separation and first-stop name but never asserts the last stop appears. The fix is a single loop-bound change plus one new test case.

Both codelines share the same stack: TypeScript 5.6 with `strict: true`, ES2022 modules, vitest 2.1. Commands in each codeline: `npm test` (vitest run), `npm run build` (tsc --noEmit). No lint is configured. Source lives under `src/`, tests under `test/`, imports use relative paths (`../src/...`).

Each fix is a one-line logic change with a corresponding one-test addition. There is no cross-codeline dependency between the two tickets.

